  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Where many observations are made of one lambda directly, as a query makes one for each element, each part of the expression which reads nothing of the argument and can change, such as a window computed from a captured clock against which every element is compared, is now observed once for all of them, as the graph observes its node for that part once: a change to what that part reads evaluates it once, and an observation is evaluated again only when the part's value changes by the equality of its type, once however many such parts the change moves. A part is taken when an evaluation first reaches it and kept while an observation which reached it remains, faults exactly the observations reading it, and is evaluated inside the raise which changed it; what it reads through something which cannot announce is still pinned by each observation as it is built, so observations share it only where they pinned the same things. A call reading nothing of the argument is therefore made once rather than once per evaluation. For a filtered query whose predicate compares each element against a window computed from a clock, a tick which leaves the window where it was went from 15.4 to 0.03 μs at 1,000 elements and from 213.2 to 0.03 μs at 10,000, and a tick which moves it costs 0.84x to 0.94x what it did. Each evaluation of a shared part allocates its value boxed, 32 bytes for a window, where a tick allocated nothing before.",
